.TH INVOKE-AUTONOMOUS-MODEL-PHASE 1 "August 2026" "autonomous-run-governance" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
invoke-autonomous-model-phase \- run one fail-closed model-routed Spec Kit phase
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B invoke-autonomous-model-phase.sh
-Action Validate|Run|Status -State PATH [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The command resolves the strongest agent-neutral routing role declared by the
installed presets, binds it to one local runner profile, and starts preflight
and phase as direct executable-plus-argument-array processes. It never uses
shell evaluation and never silently falls back to another model. Before Run
starts, the operation is persisted as NeedsRevalidation. Exit code zero alone
never completes the phase: a schema-1.0 structured result must pass semantic
validation before the operation becomes Completed.
.PP
DE: TerminalAwareRunnerAdoption gilt nur fuer die exakte Phase
implement-closeout. Ein vom Child bereits publizierter Completed/168/168-State
wird nach semantischer Resultatpruefung neu geladen und nur bei vollstaendiger
Identitaets-, Hash-, Tasks-, Git- und Closeout-Bindung adoptiert. Danach sind
Parent- und Catch-Writes auf Featurepfade null. Log und Ergebnis bleiben
runnerLocal-Evidence im gebundenen Ausgabeverzeichnis. Ein absichtlich als
Verzeichnis blockierter Logpfad bleibt nicht blockierend; ein vorhandener Log
mit falschem Pfad, Bytes oder Hash blockiert die Adoption. Andere Drift bleibt
bytegleich und verlangt read-only Reconciliation.
.PP
EN: TerminalAwareRunnerAdoption is limited to exact implement-closeout. A
child-published Completed/168/168 state is reloaded after semantic result
validation and adopted only with complete identity, hash, tasks, Git, and
closeout binding. Parent and catch feature writes are then zero. Log and result
remain runnerLocal evidence in the bound output directory. A deliberately
directory-blocked log path stays non-blocking; an existing log with the wrong
path, bytes, or hash blocks adoption. Any other drift is preserved byte-for-
byte and requires read-only reconciliation.
.PP
DE: Die Terminaladoption bindet State und Tasks an die exakten feature-lokalen
Pfade, fuehrt den installierten State-Validator aus, verlangt Completed-
Preflight und die aufgeloeste Katalog-/Profilidentitaet und verwirft Symlinks
oder Reparse Points in Leaves und Vorfahren. State und Tasks muessen exakte
HEAD-Blobs sein; Index und getrackter Worktree muessen sauber sein. Lokale und
remote Default-Refs muessen mit Fast-forward-Nachweis auf HEAD zeigen. Der
zweite TOCTOU-Tupel bindet State-, Tasks-, Result-, Payload- und Logbytes sowie
Index und getrackten Worktree.
.PP
EN: Terminal adoption binds State and Tasks to their exact feature-local
paths, runs the installed state validator, requires Completed preflight and
resolved catalog/profile identity, and rejects symlinks or reparse points in
leaves and ancestors. State and Tasks must be exact HEAD blobs; the index and
tracked worktree must be clean. Local and remote default refs must point to
HEAD with fast-forward proof. The second TOCTOU tuple binds State, Tasks,
result, payload, and log bytes plus the index and tracked worktree.
.PP
DE: Modellwechsel erfolgen nur zwischen Phasenprozessen. Konkrete Modellnamen
bleiben in der lokalen Runner-Konfiguration und ausserhalb reproduzierbarer
Feature-Anforderungen.
.PP
EN: Model changes occur only between phase processes. Concrete model names stay
in local runner configuration and outside reproducible feature requirements.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -Action
Validate checks routing and profiles, Run executes one phase, and Status reports
the persisted routing state.
.TP
.B -State PATH
Feature-local autonomous-run-state.json.
.TP
.B -RunnerConfig PATH
Local JSON file with fail-closed agent and model profiles.
.TP
.B -RoutingRoot PATH
Installed preset directory containing model-routing.json files.
.TP
.B -PhaseId ID
Stable phase identifier required by Run.
.TP
.B -Prompt TEXT
Additional non-secret phase input.
.TP
.B -WhatIf
Print the resolved phase, profile, model, and effort without starting preflight
or the phase process.
.SH SAFETY
Missing routing, profile, executable, model, effort, successful preflight, or a
valid structured result blocks execution. Script-only commands are never
started through a model profile. Success grants no commit, push, merge, bypass,
secret, deployment, Home sync, subscription, budget, cancellation, Position 7,
or provider-administration authority. Normal success without drift keeps the
parent-owned Completed write; definite child failure without drift keeps the
atomic Blocked write; uncertainty exits nonzero with
TERMINAL_STATE_DRIFT_REQUIRES_READ_ONLY_RECONCILIATION and no stale write.
.SH SEE ALSO
validate-autonomous-phase-result(1), validate-autonomous-run-state(1), orchestrate-parallel-autonomous-runs(1)
